.TH OPSEC 6 "August 20, 2026" "opsec 0.1.1" "Games"
.SH NAME
opsec \- operation-security terminal meme animation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opsec
[\fIOPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opsec
runs the OPSEC audit train, a small terminal animation for when somebody says
"install opsec" and the security team takes that literally. It is harmless:
the train crosses the terminal once and exits.
.PP
When standard output is not a terminal, one plain frame is printed instead of
using terminal control sequences.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-1 , \ \-\-once
Print one frame and exit.
.TP
.BR \-n , \ \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI colors.
.TP
.BR \-s , \ \-\-speed=MS
Set the frame delay in milliseconds. Values from 10 to 2000 are accepted.
.TP
.BR \-h , \ \-\-help
Show a short help message.
.TP
.BR \-v , \ \-\-version
Show the installed version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI colors when set to any value.
